cannot demonstrate that the exact profile implements this deny-by-default
allowlist, descriptor-rooted target binding to retained inode, and no-replace
protection, task 2.1 blocks without launching Git.

Tracked base files are then materialized without checkout through fixed
`ls-tree`/`cat-file` plumbing that reads raw blobs only. The bound base tree
contains regular `100644`/`100755` entries only; any other mode blocks.
Directory-FD-anchored no-follow/no-overwrite writes reproduce exact blob bytes
and normalized modes and fsync affected parents, so smudge/process filters,
attributes, and executable config cannot run. The approved untracked material,
snapshots, manifest, and bound sandbox profile are copied by the same contained
mechanism. A custom
inventory verifies the base tree without invoking Git conversion filters.

Post-verification requires the prestate refs/worktrees/config and every
parent-closure identity to be unchanged except for exactly one new branch ref at
the bound commit and exactly one new worktree/admin mapping at the disclosed
path with that HEAD/tree. It also verifies the reserved target identity,
worktree administrative closure, raw tracked closure, and approved untracked
hashes. Any parent swap, target replacement/occupancy, extra
ref/config/worktree/object mutation, wrong mapping, existing target, malicious
config, filter invocation, or interruption residue returns
`BLOCKED_SOURCE_WORKTREE_RECOVERY`; this approval does not authorize cleanup or
