`path_token_sha256`, `predelete_sha256`, `parent_dev`, `parent_ino`, and
`verified_absent_at`. The PASS is the atomic seal; it cannot coexist with a
missing trace, changed fingerprint/projection, `BLOCKED` cleanup, or a
different parent.

Final High Review is a later record, never a field appended to the PASS. It has
exactly `schema` (integer `1`), `kind` (`final-high-review`), `change_id`,
`major_manifest_sha256`, `parent_pass_sha256`, `reviewer`, `executor`,
`started_at`, `completed_at`, `inspected_artifact_hashes`,
`changed_file_inventory_sha256`, `critical_reruns`,
`claim_mechanism_coverage_sha256`, `adversarial_probe`,
`openspec_archive_projection_sha256`, `findings`, and `result` (`PASS`).
Reviewer and executor identities must differ. Any non-PASS finding stops
completion.

Before preliminary creation, the Router computes
`openspec_archive_projection_sha256` without changing governed source. It
hashes the exact UTF-8 prefix `openspec-archive-projection-v1` plus one NUL and
a sorted-key compact canonical inventory binding the exact archive destination,
logical change-root relocation/absence, checklist-normalized four-artifact
projection, and every affected main-spec/supporting path with predicted
post-archive type/mode/content hash. Final Review inspects that projection.
After Review, archive may perform only this transition. The Router verifies the
actual normalized inventory and strict post-archive validation, then creates an
archive receipt with exactly `schema` (integer `1`), `kind`
(`openspec-archive-receipt`), `change_id`, `major_manifest_sha256`,
`parent_review_sha256`, `expected_archive_projection_sha256`,
`actual_archive_inventory_sha256`, `strict_validation`, `archived_at`, and
`result` (`PASS`). `strict_validation` has exactly `argv`, `exit_code`,
`sanitized_result_sha256`, and `completed_at`. A mismatch or strict failure
invalidates PASS/Review and creates no receipt.

Runtime completion verifies the full preliminary/PASS/Review/archive parent
chain and fresh governed fingerprints. After the PASS seal, only new immutable
records in this closeout plane, normalized checklist progress, and the exact
Review-approved archive projection are non-invalidating; every other source/
runtime/schedule/registry/rollback/cleanup change invalidates PASS and Review.

