## Rollback

Source and runtime changes use structured backups outside discovery roots.
Because the sibling path is initially absent, rollback removes it only after
resolving and verifying the exact newly created path. Existing current-repo
files are restored from their recorded backup.

Runtime rollback unloads and removes/restores only the exact approved audit
registration, atomically restores/removes the updater discovery symlink and
immutable release according to the pre-state, and verifies that
Router/Superpowers/Companion discovery and hashes remain unchanged.

Automatic compensation during a failed apply is covered by the apply approval.
A post-success managed Skill rollback requires a new action-bound approval,
uses its receipt-bound immediately previous verified immutable release, switches
atomically, reruns target validation and discovery, and writes a rollback
receipt. Keep the current and immediately previous verified releases until a
separately approved cleanup; missing or corrupt material makes rollback
`BLOCKED`. No destructive Git or publication operation is implied.

Transaction-local staging/compensation cleanup stays within the original action
only after durable success or verified restoration. Retained post-success,
receipt-bound, rollback, or immutable-release deletion requires a new exact
cleanup plan and approval. Raw temporary debug traces follow the separate
sensitive-evidence cleanup rule above.
